  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed dwelling by reason of its location and its scale within part of an undeveloped residential garden would be an inappropriate form of development. The dwelling would form a prominent and incongruous feature that would result in a harmful impact to the character and appearance of the surrounding area. As such the proposal is contrary to policies LP1, LP5 and LP7 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and D3(1) of the London Plan (2021).\r\n",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed dwelling, by reason of its design, scale, and location, would result in an unneighbourly relationship with the adjoining property, including a loss of daylight, sunlight and outlook to the ground-floor rear bedroom window/door. The scale and proximity of the extension would cause significant harm to residential amenity, contrary to Policy LP2 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023).\r\n",
    "Reason : 3 - Insufficient information has been submitted to demonstrate how the proposal would achieve Biodiversity Net Gain (BNG). The applicant must submit a full BNG Metric and a BNG Habitat Plan, alongside a Preliminary Ecological Appraisal (PEA) that includes a bat roost assessment. The proposal therefore fails to demonstrate compliance with Policy LP55 Biodiversity of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023).\r\n",
    "Reason : 4 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to make available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal.\r\n\r\n"
  ],
